00:47:25.440 --> 00:47:28.470
that awarded him the
Presidential Medal of Science,

00:47:28.470 --> 00:47:30.280
and when you get the
Presidential Medal of Science,

00:47:30.280 --> 00:47:31.230
everyone goes to the White House.

00:47:31.230 --> 00:47:32.740
So I get invited to the White House,

00:47:32.740 --> 00:47:35.290
and here comes Riccardo
Giacconi to the White House

00:47:35.290 --> 00:47:37.020
to get the Presidential Medal of Science,

00:47:37.020 --> 00:47:40.640
and you go through the security house

00:47:40.640 --> 00:47:43.020
before you get into
the White House itself,

00:47:43.020 --> 00:47:44.920
and what does he walk through?

00:47:44.920 --> 00:47:47.350
An American Science and
Engineering metal detector.

00:47:47.350 --> 00:47:48.220
- [Chuck] Wow.

00:47:48.220 --> 00:47:50.240
- And it's like, whoa.
- And does he have a, like,

00:47:50.240 --> 00:47:53.100
metal hip or plate in his head
'cause that would be awesome.

00:47:53.100 --> 00:47:55.800
- And then they tackled him
to the ground, no. (laughs)

00:47:55.800 --> 00:47:59.290
I just thought that was
so, it brought closure

00:47:59.290 --> 00:48:01.780
to the fact that the
President is being protected

00:48:01.780 --> 00:48:03.890
by technology that he helped pioneer,

00:48:03.890 --> 00:48:05.950
and he's getting the
Presidential Medal of Science

00:48:05.950 --> 00:48:08.140
for having pioneered just that.

00:48:08.140 --> 00:48:11.249
- X-ray astronomy is a
gift that keeps on giving.

00:48:11.249 --> 00:48:12.082
- There you go.
- There it is.

00:48:12.082 --> 00:48:14.900
And I tell that story in Accessory to War

00:48:14.900 --> 00:48:18.100
with my co-author, Avis Lang.
- Nice.

00:48:18.100 --> 00:48:22.170
- And just, it's astronomy
technology affecting security

00:48:22.170 --> 00:48:25.060
- It's one more way where our penchant

00:48:25.060 --> 00:48:27.660
for trying to destroy one another has led

00:48:27.660 --> 00:48:29.833
to a modern-day marvel.

00:48:31.370 --> 00:48:33.700
- A happy note.
(group laughs)

00:48:33.700 --> 00:48:35.250
- We gotta end it there, Chuck.

00:48:36.820 --> 00:48:38.243
So Kim Arcand, thank you
for coming on StarTalk.

00:48:38.243 --> 00:48:39.730
- Thanks, yeah.
- Your first time,

00:48:39.730 --> 00:48:40.864
I hope we can get you again.
- It was fun.

00:48:40.864 --> 00:48:42.064
- [Neil] You're not
that far away, you're--

00:48:42.064 --> 00:48:43.129
- No, not at all.
- You're in Providence.

00:48:43.129 --> 00:48:45.000
- Yeah.
- Providence, Rhode Island.

00:48:45.000 --> 00:48:46.010
- Indeed.
- Yes, yes.

00:48:46.010 --> 00:48:47.447
And so it was great to
have you on the list.

00:48:47.447 --> 00:48:48.280
- Thanks.

00:48:48.280 --> 00:48:49.350
- [Neil] Chuck, always good to have you.

00:48:49.350 --> 00:48:50.460
- My pleasure, Neil.

00:48:50.460 --> 00:48:54.130
- You've been listening to,
possibly even watching StarTalk,

00:48:54.130 --> 00:48:57.520
Cosmic Queries X-ray astrophysics edition.

00:48:57.520 --> 00:48:58.950
I'm your host, Neil deGrasse Tyson,

00:48:58.950 --> 00:49:02.534
and as always, I bid
you to keep looking up.

00:49:02.534 --> 00:49:05.617
(upbeat funky music)

